  "body": "### TL;DR\r\n\r\nThis PR intent to set up the infrastructure needed to **avoid visual regressions**.\r\nIt's using [Argos CI](https://www.argos-ci.com) service under the hood. It's 100% free for open source project.\r\n\r\n### Problem solved\r\n\r\nArgos-CI's mission is to give developers the insight needed to quickly iterating on UIs. Quickly iterating on UIs involves confidence and speed of iteration.\r\nWhat we have today is a simple screenshots comparison tools that aim to solve the problem of managing those screenshots. You get:\r\n- Smart comparison: choosing the right screenshots to compare against and the diffing logic. \r\n- Github PR feedback\r\n- Acceptance and rejection action button.\r\n\r\n### Why should we care?\r\n\r\nThe promise is to catch visual regression sooner with less effort. Also, visual regression and functional regression have a positive intersection, for instance, if you have a look at [the first diff of this build](https://www.argos-ci.com/oliviertassinari/instantsearch.js/builds/3690?sample) (Doctolib UI example) you will see a visual regression at the surface but the root cause was a major functional regression: the availabilities system was broken.\r\n\r\nIt's flexible enough to fit into three categories of regressions use case I have seen:\r\n- Component as input\r\n- functional tests as input (implemented here)\r\n- pages as input\r\n\r\n### Result\r\n\r\n- Take screenshots during the functional test.\r\n![capture d ecran 2017-05-26 a 20 36 48](https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/3165635/26507980/16980e56-4253-11e7-8a60-9e30161f7907.png)\r\n- Push those screenshots for processing to Argos CI:  [build example](https://www.argos-ci.com/oliviertassinari/SplitMe/builds/3694).\r\n- We have our first notification, only admins can accept the diffs if they think it's expected.\r\n![capture d ecran 2017-05-27 a 19 31 35](https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/3165635/26523224/23af1de4-4313-11e7-9704-541e16a2ec7d.png)\r\n\r\n\r\n### API\r\n\r\nWe are using [webdriverio](https://github.com/webdriverio/webdriverio/) and [wdio-visual-regression-service](https://github.com/zinserjan/wdio-visual-regression-service).\r\nThe API is quite simple, we can leverage 3 methods to extend the coverage. It's documented [here](https://github.com/zinserjan/wdio-visual-regression-service#usage).\r\nAlternatively, we could also take screenshots outside of the functional tests.",
